<body>

<h1>Cidofovir</h1>

<div class="diamond-item">Uses:</div>
<ul>
  <li>CMV-induced retinitis in patients with AIDS</li>
</ul>

<div class="spacer"></div>

<div class="diamond-item">Adverse effects:</div>
<ul>
  <li>Dose related kidney damage</li>
  <li>Neutropenia, metabolic acidosis, uveitis and ocular hypotony also occur</li>
</ul>

<ul>
  <li><span class="note-label">Note:</span> Probenecid must be coadministered with cidofovir to reduce the risk of nephrotoxicity, but probenecid itself causes rash, headache, fever, and nausea</li>
</ul>

<div class="diamond-item">Contraindications:</div>
<ul>
  <li>Patients with preexisting renal impairment</li>
  <li>Patients taking concurrent nephrotoxic drugs, including NSAIDS</li>
</ul>

</body>
